00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:54.470
We think that,
that this something that will be valuable.

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:58.740
But already start putting myself
out there into, on the supply side.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:02.740
&gt;&gt; So there's a whole set of product
risk here which I think you guys

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:03.700
will work through.

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:05.810
The thing I keep coming back to is
actually the market risk on this.

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:10.280
because my first startup was in education,
so I know a ton about this space actually.

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:15.660
And historically the challenge has
been that they way that the average

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:19.210
person in the US thinks about things like
college admissions is actually pretty

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:24.490
different from people who are in this room
probably think about college education.

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:27.800
And fundamentally a lot of that comes
down to do you think about education

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.300
as an investment or an expenditure and

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:32.580
this happens in a lot of markets
where you kind of build for yourself.

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:36.470
And then you realize the market doesn't
actually behave the way that you behave.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:40.020
And so there's a leap that sometimes
companies aren't able to make.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:42.130
And so
that's why I was sort of probing on it.

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:45.040
I was like has the market
actually underneath this changed?

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:48.150
Like have you actually validated that
people want the same things you want?

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:50.400
And that that market is large enough
to actually support a business.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:53.090
&gt;&gt; Well actually,
there is reason change that I think,

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:56.180
will give us a opportunity
which is a new administration.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:08:00.028
Because we are talking about funding
cut into public school system.

00:08:00.028 --> 00:08:01.084
&gt;&gt; Uh-huh.

00:08:01.084 --> 00:08:05.160
&gt;&gt; So we would expect that the resources
that they have will be less and less.

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:08.590
And I think that is an opportunity to
educate the parents and student and

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:09.450
to promote.

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:11.250
The needs of having the college advising.

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:15.730
&gt;&gt; Got you, but
they don't currently get it today?

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:17.850
&gt;&gt; Right.
They get very minimal.

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:20.040
&gt;&gt; What resources do people have?

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.270
Because there's books,

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:26.910
there used to be sites like Volt.com
which I don't think gives advice anymore.

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:28.660
&gt;&gt; Yeah.
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH] So

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:29.810
what are they using right now?

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:31.540
&gt;&gt; Right.
So there are a lot of free sites

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:34.190
out there like college for,
they have check.

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:38.792
They have different websites that tells
them the details of the colleges that

00:08:38.792 --> 00:08:42.140
probably the application rates and
other stuff.

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:44.280
But those are not personalized for them.

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:46.805
And when we did an interview
with the users,

00:08:46.805 --> 00:08:49.915
they found it very overwhelming to go
through all these different sites.

00:08:49.915 --> 00:08:51.525
&gt;&gt; Who were the people that
you were interviewing?

00:08:51.525 --> 00:08:53.065
Where did you find those?

00:08:53.065 --> 00:08:54.755
&gt;&gt; We found them from our neighborhood.

00:08:54.755 --> 00:08:59.595
Found them from our friends kids and
basically people that we know.

00:08:59.595 --> 00:09:01.295
&gt;&gt; Yeah.
I keep coming back to this.

00:09:01.295 --> 00:09:05.240
I think specifically, this is one of the
biggest risks in the education market is

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:09.254
that the mass market is going to behave
differently than the people that you know.

00:09:09.254 --> 00:09:12.551
And so actually validating by talking to
those people what their needs are and

00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:13.616
what you want to build for

00:09:13.616 --> 00:09:17.000
those people and what they want is
actually pretty critical early on.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:19.680
Because people from your neighborhood
probably think about education very

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:20.770
similar to the way you do.

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:23.660
Or your friend's kids probably think
about education very similarly

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:24.310
to the way you do.

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:28.080
&gt;&gt; That's why every since we launched,
we try to iterate different ideas onto

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:31.400
the site to see which one
catch more of the attention.

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:35.270
So far I think we were able
to identify that one on one,

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:37.660
personalized interaction is important.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:42.830
But I think the next step we wanted to
drill down into something more specific,

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:45.850
so that we can just
focus on that one thing.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.492
&gt;&gt; Yeah.
Have you guys considered the international

00:09:47.492 --> 00:09:48.370
markets at all?

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:50.610
Is this just a U.S.
problem, or is this a global problem?

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:55.450
&gt;&gt; We thought about it.

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:57.090
There is some leads that we talked to.

00:09:57.090 --> 00:10:01.060
There's definitely the potential there for
international markets.

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:05.880
But the platform that we have built out so
far is really targeted to U.S., but

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:09.650
that doesn't really limit us
on expanding to more markets.

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:12.640
&gt;&gt; Have you thought about
going international first,

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:13.960
as opposed to U.S. first?

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:17.800
&gt;&gt; So our target was basically
States first, that was the focus.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:23.190
And in fact our website is admission.us,
so it's more like, you know.

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:27.286
But definitely again, we do know
that there are people out there,

00:10:27.286 --> 00:10:31.381
outside of the United States who
want to study here in the States and

00:10:31.381 --> 00:10:33.666
they need that information as well.

00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:37.926
We talked to advisors, as well,
from outside of the country, and

00:10:37.926 --> 00:10:41.348
there is the need, but
we don't really have an idea,

00:10:41.348 --> 00:10:44.102
you know let's target those markets yet.

00:10:44.102 --> 00:10:46.965
&gt;&gt; How many users are on
your site right now?

00:10:46.965 --> 00:10:49.800
&gt;&gt; We have about 200 students on site.

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:54.270
&gt;&gt; 200 students, and what's the common
element amongst all of them?

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:59.086
&gt;&gt; So we have 40% of those are senior,
so that tells me that they're pretty,

00:10:59.086 --> 00:11:01.995
they wait until pretty
last minute to do this.

00:11:01.995 --> 00:11:04.580
And then 25% the junior.

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:08.790
A majority of them are focusing on
computer science, and engineering,

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:12.170
math type, and business majors.

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:13.420
&gt;&gt; It sounds like you might want to,

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:17.940
and I think this is kind of what Avichal
was getting at also, is try to figure out

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:22.570
what is that core thing that they
really need, versus just like.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:27.060
Right now it seems a little abstract of,
I'm going to help you find a college, but

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:30.945
it might be something as simple as
the essay, like I need help on the essay.

00:11:30.945 --> 00:11:37.690
And just focus on that one thing, and
drive it home verses being a little bit,

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:42.215
doing some many things at once.

00:11:42.215 --> 00:11:45.381
&gt;&gt; So our mission is to basically
make sure that we provide the same

00:11:45.381 --> 00:11:47.125
opportunities for all students.

00:11:47.125 --> 00:11:48.965
That chance to go into college.

00:11:48.965 --> 00:11:52.885
And we understand that definitely
within maybe California,

00:11:52.885 --> 00:11:57.315
maybe in bigger cities that
students are more educated.

00:11:57.315 --> 00:12:00.135
They have the background of
what's the path to college.

00:12:00.135 --> 00:12:04.610
And beyond that what we are trying to do,
again you know going back to mission,

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:08.190
we want to make sure that outside
of these group of students,

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:12.340
