00:50:33.558 --> 00:50:36.610
Well, I think

00:50:36.610 --> 00:50:40.250
the main thing is establishing
a relationship with these folks.

00:50:40.250 --> 00:50:43.090
So, sitting down with them for
a little bit for, I don't know, a day or

00:50:43.090 --> 00:50:47.730
a week and get the work flow
going is one way to do it.

00:50:47.730 --> 00:50:50.540
Obviously, you can't
be everywhere at once.

00:50:50.540 --> 00:50:52.180
I think you can build a lot of products.

00:50:52.180 --> 00:50:54.750
You don't have to be right next to them.

00:50:54.750 --> 00:50:57.870
&gt;&gt; I think there's two general
classes of ways to do this.

00:50:57.870 --> 00:50:59.820
There's a qualitative and a quantitative.

00:50:59.820 --> 00:51:02.380
On a qualitative,
there's all different scales.

00:51:02.380 --> 00:51:05.640
You can literally have one
on one studies with users.

00:51:05.640 --> 00:51:08.540
You can have a form
that you create online.

00:51:08.540 --> 00:51:11.730
There's user feedback software that will
give you a bunch of qualitative feedback.

00:51:11.730 --> 00:51:14.685
And if people upload something
that gives you some signal.

00:51:14.685 --> 00:51:17.698
I've seen some companies use what
people would call a client council.

00:51:17.698 --> 00:51:20.880
&gt;&gt; For you guys you take like a
representative sample of 12 to 15 people.

00:51:20.880 --> 00:51:22.810
You bring them in once a quarter or
once every six months.

00:51:22.810 --> 00:51:23.660
You show them new stuff.

00:51:23.660 --> 00:51:26.810
They're NDA'd, they talk through it,
they give you qualitative feedback.

00:51:26.810 --> 00:51:29.780
And it's like a very targeted way
to do this all in one sitting.

00:51:29.780 --> 00:51:32.625
Then there's all the quantitative stuff,
so there's always metrics right?

00:51:32.625 --> 00:51:34.005
Ultimately your KPIs.

00:51:34.005 --> 00:51:36.085
And there's only really
four classes of metrics.

00:51:36.085 --> 00:51:37.995
There's how many people use your stuff?

00:51:37.995 --> 00:51:39.745
How deeply do they use your stuff?

00:51:39.745 --> 00:51:41.975
How good is it at doing the thing
that you say it's supposed to do and

00:51:41.975 --> 00:51:43.095
how much money do you make?

00:51:43.095 --> 00:51:45.335
And all of your metrics
basically roll into those four.

00:51:45.335 --> 00:51:48.425
And when your building features your
just mapping against those things and

00:51:48.425 --> 00:51:49.675
you see whether those numbers move.

00:51:49.675 --> 00:51:53.390
And so between those two, you should
be able to triangulate whether or

00:51:53.390 --> 00:51:54.258
not a thing is working.

